{
  "name": "BusinessDocument",
  "type": "object",
  "description": "Chapter 6 P1 \u2014 the ONE canonical business document vault record (insurance, formation, agreements, policies, registrations, permits, certifications, professional documents \u2014 no separate vaults). Files live in PRIVATE storage (file_uri); viewing/downloading always goes through a short-lived signed URL. The document owns its expiration_date; a missing expiration_date means NO EXPIRATION KNOWN (never 'never expires'). version is the acknowledgment-truth anchor: it increments when the file is replaced, so an old acknowledgment never silently covers a new version. Chapter 16 P1-25 adds the 'item' scope so a client-provided APPRAISAL (or other item evidence document) attaches to a canonical Item \u2014 no Appraisal entity; an appraisal is EVIDENCE/CONTEXT and its value is never copied into Item.price. Chapter 25 P1 adds the knowledge block (structured SOP/company-knowledge lifecycle) and the SOP/TRAINING/CHECKLIST categories \u2014 no second SOP entity; file_uri is no longer required because a structured procedure record may be fileless (uploaded files keep it).",
  "properties": {
    "operator_id": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Estate Sale Company Owner user ID (RLS anchor)."
    },
    "company_id": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Canonical Company when known (additive projection)."
    },
    "title": {
      "type": "string"
    },
    "category": {
      "type": "string",
      "enum": [
        "FORMATION",
        "INSURANCE",
        "AGREEMENT",
        "POLICY",
        "REGISTRATION",
        "PERMIT",
        "CERTIFICATION",
        "PROFESSIONAL",
        "APPRAISAL",
        "SOP",
        "TRAINING",
        "CHECKLIST",
        "OTHER"
      ],
      "default": "OTHER",
      "description": "Document category. Deliberately small taxonomy. Chapter 16 APPRAISAL = a client-provided or commissioned appraisal document attached to an Item \u2014 evidence/context only, never a price the system applies. Chapter 25 P1 adds SOP (a structured operating procedure), TRAINING, and CHECKLIST \u2014 these carry the knowledge block lifecycle; there is no second SOP repository."
    },
    "policy_type": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "For POLICY documents only: e.g. Confidentiality Policy, Safety Policy, Team Policy, Photo / Privacy Policy, Sale-Day Procedure."
    },
    "scope": {
      "type": "string",
      "enum": [
        "business",
        "sale",
        "contact",
        "team_member",
        "item"
      ],
      "default": "business",
      "description": "Explicit scope. sale_id / contact_id / team_member_id / item_id must match this scope (enforced by the vault UI \u2014 one ref per scope, never contradictory combinations). Chapter 16 P1-25 'item' scope attaches an item-scoped evidence document (e.g. an appraisal) to a canonical Item."
    },
    "sale_id": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "EstateSale ID when scope is 'sale'."
    },
    "contact_id": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Contact ID when scope is 'contact'."
    },
    "team_member_id": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "TeamMember ID when scope is 'team_member'."
    },
    "item_id": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Chapter 16 P1-25 \u2014 canonical Item ID when scope is 'item' (e.g. an appraisal attached to specific merchandise). The Item remains the merchandise record; this document is private evidence only."
    },
    "file_uri": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "PRIVATE storage URI (UploadPrivateFile). Never a public URL. Chapter 25 P1: optional \u2014 a structured SOP/knowledge record may be fileless; uploaded files keep it."
    },
    "file_name": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Original filename at upload."
    },
    "effective_date": {
      "type": "string",
      "format": "date"
    },
    "expiration_date": {
      "type": "string",
      "format": "date",
      "description": "The document owns this date. Null = NO EXPIRATION KNOWN (not 'never expires')."
    },
    "status": {
      "type": "string",
      "enum": [
        "ACTIVE",
        "ARCHIVED",
        "REVIEW"
      ],
      "default": "ACTIVE",
      "description": "No status implies a legal retention conclusion. Distinct from the Chapter 25 knowledge lifecycle (knowledge.sop_status): a CURRENT approved SOP is ACTIVE + sop_status APPROVED; an archived one is ARCHIVED."
    },
    "notes": {
      "type": "string"
    },
    "version": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 1,
      "description": "Incremented when the file is replaced. Acknowledgment truth anchor: an acknowledgment records the version acknowledged, so a replaced policy is never silently considered acknowledged. Chapter 25 P1: SOP revisions create a NEW record (knowledge.supersedes_document_id) with version = previous + 1, so prior approved versions are preserved as SUPERSEDED, never overwritten."
    },
    "template_text": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Chapter 9 P0 \u2014 for operator-designated AGREEMENT templates only: the operator's own attorney-reviewed agreement TEXT containing {{MERGE_VARIABLE}} placeholders (e.g. {{CLIENT_NAME}}, {{COMMISSION_RATE}}). EstateSalen populates approved variables from structured records; it never authors, edits, or AI-generates legal language, and a placeholder with no source is flagged MISSING VALUE \u2014 never fabricated."
    },
    "knowledge": {
      "type": "object",
      "default": {},
      "description": "Chapter 25 P1 \u2014 the COMPANY KNOWLEDGE / SOP lifecycle block. A DRAFT PROCEDURE IS NOT APPROVED POLICY: only the explicit human approval path (companyKnowledge 'approve' \u2014 operator/admin only) writes sop_status APPROVED, and AI can never set approval truth (ai_generated drafts stay DRAFT until a human approves). Employees never read the operator's vault directly: the companyKnowledge server seam is the ONLY employee surface, and it returns ONLY employee_visible APPROVED records as safe projections. employee_visible defaults false \u2014 fail-safe; nothing becomes employee knowledge implicitly.",
      "properties": {
        "sop_status": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "DRAFT",
            "IN_REVIEW",
            "APPROVED",
            "SUPERSEDED"
          ],
          "description": "Chapter 25 P1 \u2014 the SOP/knowledge lifecycle. DRAFT/IN_REVIEW are operator-private working states. APPROVED = the CURRENT human-approved version (at most ONE APPROVED version per procedure lineage \u2014 approving supersedes the previous APPROVED record). SUPERSEDED = a prior approved version, preserved for history, never deleted or rewritten."
        },
        "purpose": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "WHAT IS THIS PROCEDURE FOR? One or two plain sentences."
        },
        "audience_roles": {
          "type": "array",
          "default": [],
          "description": "Chapter 19 role vocabulary reuse (NO parallel role system). Empty = all staff of the company. Restricts which employees the knowledge seam surfaces this record to (server-side filter, never just UI).",
          "items": {
            "type": "string",
            "enum": [
              "ENTRY",
              "CHECKOUT",
              "FLOOR_ZONE",
              "HIGH_VALUE",
              "NEGOTIATION",
              "FURNITURE",
              "PICKUP",
              "CUSTOMER_ISSUES",
              "SALE_FLOOR_RECOVERY",
              "ALL_STAFF"
            ]
          }
        },
        "steps": {
          "type": "array",
          "default": [],
          "description": "The NORMAL PATH \u2014 ordered plain steps. Structured content, deliberately not a workflow engine.",
          "items": {
            "type": "object",
            "properties": {
              "text": {
                "type": "string"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "decision_points": {
          "type": "array",
          "default": [],
          "description": "IF X \u2192 DO Y / IF NOT \u2192 DO Z. Advisory structured branches for humans \u2014 never auto-executed.",
          "items": {
            "type": "object",
            "properties": {
              "condition": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "if_yes": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "if_no": {
                "type": "string"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "exceptions": {
          "type": "array",
          "default": [],
          "description": "When the normal path does NOT apply.",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "escalation": {
          "type": "object",
          "description": "WHEN TO STOP, WHO/WHICH ROLE to escalate to, and WHAT INFORMATION to provide. Reuses the Chapter 19 Ask-for-Help path \u2014 the procedure makes escalation visible but NEVER grants authority.",
          "properties": {
            "stop_when": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "escalate_to": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "provide": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          }
        },
        "completion_standard": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "WHAT MUST BE TRUE before this procedure is finished. A procedure without an ending is not a complete procedure."
        },
        "change_reason": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "WHY this version exists (near miss, recurring issue, employee improvement, client problem, efficiency, successful practice, policy change...)."
        },
        "supersedes_document_id": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "The prior version's BusinessDocument ID this revision replaces. Approving this record supersedes that one (SUPERSEDED)."
        },
        "approved_by": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "User ID of the authorized human who approved. HUMAN APPROVAL ONLY \u2014 AI and employee suggestions can never set approval truth."
        },
        "approved_by_name": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "approved_at": {
          "type": "string",
          "format": "date-time"
        },
        "review_date": {
          "type": "string",
          "format": "date",
          "description": "Effectiveness review date \u2014 did this change actually help? A date on the record; no automated mining."
        },
        "effectiveness_reviews": {
          "type": "array",
          "default": [],
          "description": "Human assessments recorded at review. History preserved; earlier reviews never rewritten.",
          "items": {
            "type": "object",
            "properties": {
              "at": {
                "type": "string",
                "format": "date-time"
              },
              "outcome": {
                "type": "string",
                "enum": [
                  "BETTER",
                  "NO_CHANGE",
                  "WORSE",
                  "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE"
                ]
              },
              "note": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "by_name": {
                "type": "string"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "source_type": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "EMPLOYEE_OBSERVATION",
            "SALE_ISSUE",
            "NEAR_MISS",
            "SALE_RECAP",
            "MANAGER_OBSERVATION",
            "MANUAL"
          ],
          "default": "MANUAL",
          "description": "Provenance \u2014 where this procedure/improvement came from."
        },
        "source_id": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Canonical source record ID (SaleIssue, SaleRecap...) when applicable."
        },
        "source_label": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Short human label of the source \u2014 no sensitive full text copied."
        },
        "contributor_name": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Knowledge attribution \u2014 who contributed the lesson (employee experience should survive the employee)."
        },
        "ai_generated": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "default": false,
          "description": "Chapter 24 governance \u2014 an AI-DRAFTED procedure is labeled as such forever; it still requires explicit human approval and never becomes policy on its own."
        },
        "employee_visible": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "default": false,
          "description": "Explicit operator choice to publish this record to the employee knowledge surface. False = stays operator-private even when APPROVED. Fail-safe default."
        }
      }
    },
    "uploaded_by": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "User ID of the uploader."
    },
    "reminders_sent": {
      "type": "array",
      "default": [],
      "description": "Reminder-engine idempotency ledger. Each warning window (60/30/7/expired) fires at most once per document; a second daily run creates no duplicate notification.",
      "items": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "window": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "sent_date": {
            "type": "string",
            "format": "date"
          }
        }
      }
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "operator_id",
    "title",
    "category"
  ],
  "rls": {
    "read": {
      "$or": [
        {
          "data.operator_id": "{{user.id}}"
        },
        {
          "user_condition": {
            "role": "admin"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    "create": {
      "$or": [
        {
          "data.operator_id": "{{user.id}}"
        },
        {
          "user_condition": {
            "role": "admin"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    "update": {
      "$or": [
        {
          "data.operator_id": "{{user.id}}"
        },
        {
          "user_condition": {
            "role": "admin"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    "delete": {
      "$or": [
        {
          "data.operator_id": "{{user.id}}"
        },
        {
          "user_condition": {
            "role": "admin"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}